.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Pollard&#x27;s rho method finds a prime factor p of n in roughly \sqrt p steps, by waiting for a birthday-paradox collision in the sequence x \mapsto x^2 + 1 \bmod p. This script factors the Fermat number F_6 = 2^{64}+1 and plots the step count against the smallest prime factor for a batch of semiprimes.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/number_theory/factorization/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_pollard_rho_thumb.png
